WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Agulhas retroflection. Surface particles follow HYCOM's evolving horizontal velocity field. Color gives speed in meters per second; seed density is not transport. Model time: 30 September–4 October 2026. Relief is exaggerated 60 times in the first three chapters.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
Vertical relative vorticity: blue is clockwise, coral is counterclockwise. Color measures local rotation; it does not classify eddy boundaries. Pearl paths follow the modeled horizontal velocity.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
48-hour forward finite-time Lyapunov exponent, starting 30 September 2026 and ending 2 October. Brighter colors show stronger modeled trajectory separation. The field is held fixed as the camera moves.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
Surface, 200-meter and 1,000-meter horizontal trajectories. Each particle stays on its sampled depth surface. The comparison uses daily temporal samples. Vertical display scale is exaggerated 160 times. No vertical velocity is reconstructed.
